## Open the workbench

The workbench is opened from a bookkeeping case. A case belongs to one company and one period (a quarter, or a financial year for annual bookkeeping).

1. Open the company, or find the case on the board.
2. If no case exists for the period, select **Start a bookkeeping case**.
3. Open the case to show the workbench.

{% screenshot id="bookkeeping/getting-started-case-entry" caption="A bookkeeping case for ABC PTE. LTD., Q3 2026." /%}

The company page also has a **Books** tab. It is read-only: it shows the general ledger, the trial balance, the financial statements, the GST returns and the source documents as they stand. To change the books, open a case.

## Who can see the books

The books of a case can be read only by the participants of the case. Another member of the firm can see that the case exists, but cannot open its books until added as a participant. A company can also be restricted to an access list; then only the members of that list can open its books.

## Who does what

| Role | Work |
|---|---|
| **Preparer** (for example, Demo Accountant) | Uploads and reads the documents, answers the to-do items, reconciles the bank accounts, books the period-end adjustments and submits the work for review. |
| **Reviewer** (a manager, for example Demo Manager) | Signs off the bank reconciliations, reviews the manual changes, confirms the F5 and completes the period. |

A manager cannot sign off work that the same manager prepared: another reviewer must sign it off. Overriding a quarter check, completing a period and reopening a completed period are reserved for managers.

{% aside type="note" %}
The AI employee does most of the first pass: it reads the documents, answers the to-do items once and matches the bank lines. Every decision it makes is listed under **Reconcile › Answered**, where the preparer checks it. See [Step 2 · Journal](/en/bookkeeping/journal/).
{% /aside %}
